nominal limit: 10 requests per second; 64 requests arrive

  limiter                   admitted  most in one second   state kept
  fixed window                    60                  20   one counter
  sliding log                     49                  10   a timestamp per request
  token bucket, burst 10          50                  10   two numbers
  token bucket, burst 3           43                  10   two numbers

The fixed window admitted twice its limit inside one second, by taking a full
allowance on each side of a boundary. The sliding log never exceeds the limit and
pays with memory; the token bucket is close to it with two numbers of state, and its
burst size is the dial between absorbing a spike and smoothing it.
